            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0426" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.796/19: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-07T23:00:00-04:00">October 7, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>254. Your 314, September 30. War Department states that permission was granted to
                    the British to refuel at Fisherman’s Lake and to station a few men in civilian
                    clothes there but that it was not the intent of the War Department to grant the
                    British anything in the way of a permanent or large-scale installation. War
                    Department is discussing the matter with British air representatives in
                    Washington and you will be advised as to the results.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
